---
pagination:
  data: trades
  size: 1
  alias: t
  # Without this Eleventy adds ONLY the first paginated page to collections,
  # so the sitemap would list one trade page and silently omit the rest.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/"
# `| safe` on every passthrough is load-bearing, not decoration. These strings
# are rendered here and then rendered AGAIN by whatever outputs them (the layout,
# the meta tags, the schema). Without `safe` an apostrophe is escaped to `&#39;`
# on this pass and the `&` is escaped to `&amp;` on the next, so the page shows
# a literal "website&#39;s". Escaping belongs at the point of output, once.
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ t.title | safe }}"
  description: "{{ t.description | safe }}"
  eyebrow: "FOR {{ t.plural | upper | safe }}"
  heading: "{{ t.heading | safe }}"
  intro: "{{ t.intro | safe }}"
  breadcrumbName: "Websites for {{ t.plural | safe }}"
---
{% extends "layouts/page.njk" %}

{% block schema %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Service",
        "@id": "{{ site.url }}/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/#service",
        "name": "Website design for {{ t.plural }}",
        "serviceType": "Website design for {{ t.plural }} in New Zealand",
        "provider": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#business" },
        "description": {{ t.description | dump | safe }},
        "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "New Zealand" },
        "audience": {
          "@type": "BusinessAudience",
          "name": "New Zealand {{ t.plural }}"
        },
        "offers": {
          "@type": "Offer",
          "price": "{{ site.price }}",
          "priceCurrency": "{{ site.currency }}",
          "availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
          "url": "{{ site.url }}/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/",
          "seller": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@id": "{{ site.url }}/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/#faq",
        "mainEntity": [{% for item in t.faqs %}
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": {{ item.q | dump | safe }},
            "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | dump | safe }} }
          }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
{% endblock %}

{% block prose %}
<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>{{ site.priceDisplay }} flat, live in {{ site.buildDays }}.</strong> Copywriting, local SEO, .nz domain and Google Business Profile setup included — with the Jobs In {{ site.guaranteeDays }} Guarantee. If it doesn't bring you a genuine job enquiry in {{ site.guaranteeDays }} days, we rebuild it free.</p>
</div>

<h2>How your customers actually search</h2>
<p>{{ t.howTheySearch }}</p>

<h2>What's costing {{ t.plural }} work right now</h2>
{%- for p in t.painPoints %}
<h3>{{ p.title }}</h3>
<p>{{ p.body }}</p>
{%- endfor %}

<h2>The pages a {{ t.slang }}'s website needs</h2>
<p>Your build is five or more pages. For {{ t.plural }}, these are the ones that earn their place:</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>Why it's there</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {%- for pg in t.pagesYouNeed %}
      <tr><td><strong>{{ pg.name }}</strong></td><td>{{ pg.why }}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2>The trust signals we put front and centre</h2>
<p>These are what a {{ t.slang }} has that an amateur doesn't. Most {{ t.plural }}' websites hide them in the footer:</p>
<ul>
  {%- for s in t.trustSignals %}
  <li>{{ s }}</li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>The kind of copy we'd write for you</h2>
<p>You don't write a word of this. We interview you for 30 minutes and write the lot. For a {{ t.slang }}, the homepage headline tends to land somewhere like:</p>
<div class="sample-copy">
  <p class="sample-headline">{{ t.exampleHeadline }}</p>
  <p class="sample-sub">{{ t.exampleSub }}</p>
</div>
<p>Yours will be specific to your business, your area and the work you actually want more of — not this, with your name dropped in.</p>

<h2>Questions from {{ t.plural }}</h2>
{%- for item in t.faqs %}
<h3>{{ item.q }}</h3>
<p>{{ item.a }}</p>
{%- endfor %}
<p>More on the <a href="/faq/">general FAQ</a>, and the full terms of both guarantees on the <a href="/guarantee/">guarantee page</a>.</p>

<hr />

<h2>What it costs</h2>
<p><strong>{{ site.priceDisplay }}</strong>, one time. That covers the build, all copywriting, the local SEO foundation, your .nz domain, {{ site.hostingIncluded }}, and Google Business Profile setup. The first ten founding clients pay {{ site.foundingPriceDisplay }}.</p>
<p>Full breakdown, including what it costs to do this another way, on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>.</p>

<h2>Ready to go?</h2>
<p>Book a kickoff call. Thirty minutes, and we'll tell you honestly whether a website will move the needle for a {{ t.slang }} in your area — including if the answer is no.</p>
<p><a href="/#contact" class="btn large">BOOK MY KICKOFF CALL →</a></p>

<hr />

<h2>We also build for</h2>
<ul class="trade-links">
  {%- for other in trades %}{% if other.slug != t.slug %}
  <li><a href="/websites-for-{{ other.slug }}/">Websites for {{ other.plural }}</a></li>
  {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p>Not on the list? We build for every trade — <a href="/#contact">tell us yours</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
